Hash: SHA512

annotations:
  artifacthub.io/changes: |
    - kind: changed
      description: "Updated the edge image to 4.12.0, which sets its Go memory limit from the container's memory limit: 90% of edge.resources.limits.memory, less the memory outside the Go runtime (mostly the WURFL device-detection data), recomputed every minute so it follows an in-place resize. Near that limit the garbage collector runs more often instead of letting the heap grow to twice the live data, so a busy edge with a full natural-width store is far less likely to be OOMKilled. No new value; an explicit GOMEMLIMIT in edge.env still wins. See docs/SIZING.md, \"Edge memory and the natural-width store\"."
    - kind: added
      description: "helm install and helm upgrade now fail when edge.resources.limits.memory can't hold a full natural-width store of edge.env.EDGE_WIDTH_CACHE_SIZE entries: (400 MiB + 180 bytes per entry) must stay within 85% of the limit. A store too big for its limit runs fine until it fills, days later or within seconds with Edge Warm Start, and then the edge is OOMKilled. The message gives the limit to set, or the largest store that fits. The defaults (2.5M entries, 1Gi) pass; an unset EDGE_WIDTH_CACHE_SIZE counts as the edge's default of 5M, which needs about 1.5Gi. See docs/SIZING.md, \"Edge memory and the natural-width store\"."
  artifacthub.io/signKey: |
